From 191a0543177fcb2097c8012e87342a49a5d5b557 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:59:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix data-exposure issues: password hashes, open endpoints,
 default creds
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Move password verification/updates for change-password and reset-password
  (both token and forced-reset modes) into server-side API routes. The
  browser no longer fetches password_hash at all; bcrypt compare/hash now
  happens only in lib/supabase-admin.ts-backed routes, using the NextAuth
  session (not a client-supplied email) to establish identity.
- Add lib/auth-options.ts so getServerSession() can be used from API routes,
  and lib/supabase-admin.ts as a server-only Supabase client (prefers
  SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY, warns if it falls back to the anon key).
- UserManagementTab: stop selecting password_hash (and the rest of `*`) into
  the admin user list; select only the columns the table actually renders.
  Also fix the self-delete guard, which called supabase.auth.getSession()
  and always got back an empty session (this app uses NextAuth, not
  Supabase Auth), so the "can't delete your own account" check never
  actually fired — now uses the real NextAuth session.
- Require an authenticated admin/super_admin session on /api/send-email
  (previously anyone could use it as an open mail relay from the app's
  domain) and a shared-secret check on /api/cron/check-notifications
  (previously anyone who found the URL could trigger it, spamming admins
  and burning the service-role-authenticated Supabase/Resend calls inside
  it).
- lib/email.ts: sendPasswordResetEmail() read its Resend key from
  NEXT_PUBLIC_RESEND_API_KEY, which would ship a secret API key into the
  client bundle if this function is ever called from the browser. Renamed
  to the server-only RESEND_API_KEY already used everywhere else.
- scripts/setup-auth.ts: generate a random password per seeded account
  instead of the hardcoded FlightPro@2024 (which was committed, in plain
  text, to this public repo). Removed the stray `code` scratch file that
  hashed the same literal password. scripts/test-auth.ts now uses an
  obviously-fake placeholder instead of the real default password.
- Add .env.example (and un-ignore it) documenting every env var these
  routes need, including the new CRON_SECRET.

Note: this does not change how the rest of the app reads/writes Supabase
tables from the browser using the anon key — that's the bigger
access-control/RLS question flagged separately and intentionally left for
a follow-up pass.
